description:
Business Unit
Tencent Games was established in 2003. We are a leading global platform for game development, operations and publishing, and the largest online game community in China.
Tencent Games has developed and operated over 140 games. We provide cross-platform interactive entertainment experience for more than 800 million users in over 200 countries and regions around the world. Honor of Kings, PUBG MOBILE, and League of Legends, are some of our most popular titles around the world.
Meanwhile, we actively promote the development of esports industry, work with global partners to build an open, collaborative and symbiotic industrial ecology, and create high-quality digital life experiences for players.

About the Hiring Team
Game Research Center(GRC) is a department focusing on game industry study, game analysis, game design research, data analysis and game development supporting. We’re one of the world’s leading research facility in game industry, building a global knowledge tank to help our teams make better decisions. We’re looking for innovative and passionate team members who love all kinds of games and have insight about the challenging global market.

What the Role Entails

Responsibilities

1. Track game market trends across Europe and the broader Western market, producing regular reports on genre trends, competitive landscape, and industry developments;

2. Support investment evaluation of overseas game projects, conducting market-level competitive analysis and commercial viability assessments on target titles and studios;

3. Monitor and analyze key game products on an ongoing basis, delivering structured product observations and market insights;

4. Participate in industry events and trade shows, synthesizing on-the-ground findings into comprehensive event and market reports;

5. Assist in building and maintaining market intelligence assets, ensuring systematic data accumulation and continuous updates.

Who We Look For

Requirements

1. 3–5 years of relevant experience; background in finance, consulting, market research, or investment analysis preferred; prior experience in the games industry, especially in AI//UGC/Shooter is a plus;

2. Solid understanding of the European and North American gaming market, with familiarity with mainstream market data platforms and analytical tools;

3. Strong structured thinking and report writing skills, with the ability to translate data into actionable business insights;

4. Genuine passion for games with extensive play experience, capable of forming independent judgments on product quality and market reception;

5. English as primary working language; proficiency in Chinese is a plus.

Equal Employment Opportunity at Tencent

As an equal opportunity employer, we firmly believe that diverse voices fuel our innovation and allow us to better serve our users and the community. We foster an environment where every employee of Tencent feels supported and inspired to achieve individual and common goals.

Business Unit
Tencent Games was established in 2003. We are a leading global platform for game development, operations and publishing, and the largest online game community in China.
Tencent Games has developed and operated over 140 games. We provide cross-platform interactive entertainment experience for more than 800 million users in over 200 countries and regions around the world. Honor of Kings, PUBG MOBILE, and League of Legends, are some of our most popular titles around the world.
Meanwhile, we actively promote the development of esports industry, work with global partners to build an open, collaborative and symbiotic industrial ecology, and create high-quality digital life experiences for players.

About the Hiring Team
Game Research Center(GRC) is a department focusing on game industry study, game analysis, game design research, data analysis and game development supporting. We’re one of the world’s leading research facility in game industry, building a global knowledge tank to help our teams make better decisions. We’re looking for innovative and passionate team members who love all kinds of games and have insight about the challenging global market.

What the Role Entails

Responsibilities:

1. In-depth evaluation of game projects in the European market, assessing product quality, studio capabilities, and competitive positioning to deliver high-quality analytical reports;

2. Deep expertise in core European game genres, with a particular specialization in FPS; capable of independently assessing a title's fundamental strengths and challenges at any stage of development;

3. Provide full-cycle tracking and coverage of key partner projects, offering professional input and directional recommendations tailored to each stage of development;

4. Represent the team at major industry events and external engagements, building and sustaining professional relationships with overseas developers and publishers;

5. Deliver strategically valuable genre insights and competitive landscape analyses from both a market and product perspective, informing the team's overall decision-making.

Who We Look For

Requirements

1. 5+ years of experience in the games industry, with a background in game development, production, design, or publishing evaluation across console, PC, or mobile platforms; experience in the European or broader Western market strongly preferred;

2. Demonstrate deep expertise in key game genres across the European market, with specialised experience and a strong understanding of the shooter genre in particular. Able to independently and professionally assess core product challenges at different stages of a project lifecycle.

3. Excellent report writing and analytical skills, capable of owning the full pipeline from information gathering to actionable conclusions;

4. Strong cross-functional collaboration and project coordination abilities, comfortable operating in a fast-paced, multi-track work environment;

5. English as primary working language; willingness to travel for overseas business trips and industry events required.

Equal Employment Opportunity at Tencent

As an equal opportunity employer, we firmly believe that diverse voices fuel our innovation and allow us to better serve our users and the community. We foster an environment where every employee of Tencent feels supported and inspired to achieve individual and common goals.
